  "derivation": "LRM 7.6.2 Example 7 on \"Hello, world, and good bye!\" (27 bytes): [..4] = Hello, [7..11] = world, [1] = e; find(world) = 7, find(earth) = -1, find(o) = 4, find(o, 6) = 8, find_last(o) = 20; [7..] is 20 bytes. format_string(\"%s-%d\", \"WORLD\", 7) = WORLD-7. The compares read contents, not identity: s1, s4 and s5 are built at run time and equal the literals."
